<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Aspern-Essling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1809</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-fifth-coalition">War of the Fifth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Aspern-Essling was fought on 21–22 May 1809 on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, where Archduke Charles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> repulsed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s attempt to cross the river. It was the first major defeat of Napoleon in person in more than a decade, though he recrossed the Danube and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wagram">Battle of Wagram</a> six weeks later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-aspern-essling.jpg" alt="Battle of Aspern-Essling" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Peter Krafft · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archduke_Charles,_Duke_of_Teschen,_with_his_Staff_at_the_Battle_of_Aspern-Essling,_21%E2%80%9322_May_1809_(by_Johann_Peter_Krafft,_1820).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
